    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 051041\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n241 AM PST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Northerly winds will pick up Friday and Saturday, with stronger\n  speeds and elevated wave heights along the Colorado River\n  Valley. Otherwise, quiet conditions.\n\n&&\n\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Wednesday.\n\nHeights will drop and clouds will increase this afternoon as a \nresult of an approaching shortwave, which will keep temperatures \nbelow-normal for another day. This shortwave will continue to \nstrengthen as it sags southward before closing off on Friday over \ncentral Arizona. Meanwhile, a growing ridge of high pressure in the \neastern Pacific Ocean will nose into the Great Basin, allowing \ntemperatures to gradually climb late-week into the weekend. The \nincreased pressure gradients as a result of a ridge to our north and \na closed low to our southeast will bring gusty north winds to the \nforecast area on Friday and Saturday with speeds generally between \n15 and 25 mph. However, due to topographic enhancement along the \nColorado River Valley, expect locally higher sustained wind speeds \nof 15 to 25 mph and gusts to 40 mph. A Lake Wind Advisory has been \nissued for Lake Mohave and Lake Havasu from early Friday morning \nthrough Saturday afternoon as a result, with expected wave heights \nbetween 2 and 3 feet. Heights continue to rise over the region \nthrough the remainder of the weekend and into next week, resulting \nin dry conditions and gradually warming temperatures.\n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Light \nwinds will persist through today and tonight. Expect northeast \nwinds this afternoon at 040-050 degrees (true) but speeds will \nlikely remain under 8KT through the afternoon. Winds will shift to\na typical overnight wind direction at sunset before going back to\nthe northwest around 8KT around 09Z. Friday morning around \nsunrise, north to northwest winds will increase to around 10KT and\ngusts up to 20KT are expected to develop. VFR skies are expected \nthrough the period. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...In general, light winds \nfavoring the north to northwest through much of the period. The \nexception will be the Colorado River Valley where north winds will \ngust 20-25KT this afternoon. Winds in the Colorado River Valley will \ndiminish slightly this evening but will continue at about 10KT with \noccasional gusts 15-20KT through the night into Friday morning. \nMostly clear VFR skies are expected through the period. \n&&\n\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Soulat\nAVIATION...Nickerson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
